## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## We deliberately leave the BEAM break handler enabled (no +Bd).
## - For the TUI, the bridge NIF puts the terminal in raw mode before
##   Ctrl+C can become a SIGINT, so the break menu never shows.
## - For `serve`, we want Ctrl+C to stop the server. `+Bd` disables the
##   menu but ALSO causes SIGINT to be ignored entirely (OTP reserves
##   SIGINT; :os.set_signal(:sigint, :handle) is not permitted). Losing
##   the ability to Ctrl+C the server is worse than the one-line menu.
